#usda 1.0
(
    doc = """Xform-import fixture (task 1.2): NO defaultPrim authored, and more
    than one prim at the top level.

    The importer always roots the imported tree at the stage's pseudo-root, so
    this file is not an exceptional path -- it is the case that proves the rule
    holds when there is genuinely no defaultPrim to fall back from, AND that
    multiple top-level prims all survive the import. (defaultPrim is a
    *referencing* hint -- "which prim does a reference to this layer target?"
    (layer.h:831-833) -- not a declaration that the rest of the stage is
    unimportant, so it must not decide what gets imported.)

    The pseudo-root is not a real prim: its path is "/", its name and typeName
    are empty, and it has no xformOps.

    Expected:
      - both /First and /Second appear in the imported tree, parented under a
        single synthetic root node; /Second/SecondChild nests below /Second
      - the synthetic root is named from the root layer's display name, run
        through validate_node_name() -- so this file yields the node name
        "no_default_prim_usda" (the '.' is not legal in a Godot node name).
        Anonymous / in-memory layers have no display name; those fall back to
        "_root"
      - the synthetic root carries metadata like every other node:
        usd_prim_path = "/" and usd_type_name = "" (empty). Empty type is NOT
        special-cased here -- it is a legitimate value that also appears on
        typeless prims (`def "Foo" {}`), so the root is consistent with them
        rather than an exception. Consumers that specifically need the stage
        root can test usd_prim_path == "/", which is unambiguous.

    Stages exported without a defaultPrim are common in the wild, so this path
    is not an exotic edge case."""
    metersPerUnit = 1
    upAxis = "Y"
)

def Xform "First"
{
    double3 xformOp:translate = (1, 0, 0)
    uniform token[] xformOpOrder = ["xformOp:translate"]
}

def Xform "Second"
{
    double3 xformOp:translate = (0, 2, 0)
    uniform token[] xformOpOrder = ["xformOp:translate"]

    def Xform "SecondChild"
    {
    }
}
